1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,880
Have you ever made a promise to yourself that you didn’t keep?
你是否曾对自己许下承诺，最后却没能遵守？

2
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:15,070
Commonly, when the new year ticks over, we make resolutions: going to the gym, studying harder or giving up a bad habit.
通常，每当新年钟声敲响，我们都会立下新年决心：去健身房锻炼、更努力学习或是戒掉某个坏习惯。

3
00:00:15,070 --> 00:00:21,060
Sadly, not long after we’ve made the promise, we often end up breaking them.
遗憾的是，许下诺言后没过多久，我们往往就会违背它。

4
00:00:21,060 --> 00:00:24,650
But what if you want to create a new good habit?
但如果你想养成一个新的好习惯呢？

5
00:00:24,650 --> 00:00:31,160
Well, it’s possible, but willpower might not be the only thing you need.
这并非不可能，但意志力或许并非你唯一需要的东西。

6
00:00:31,160 --> 00:00:38,340
The basic idea of a habit is something we do almost unconsciously, as if you’re on autopilot.
习惯的本质，是我们近乎无意识、如同自动驾驶般做出的行为。

7
00:00:38,340 --> 00:00:43,430
An example of this would be having breakfast or saying ‘please’ and ‘thank you’.
比如吃早餐、说“请”和“谢谢”，这些都是习惯。

8
00:00:43,430 --> 00:00:46,850
Good habits can be part of your daily routine.
好习惯可以成为日常生活的一部分。

9
00:00:46,850 --> 00:00:51,790
But if we don’t have those habits, how can we create them?
但如果我们本身没有这些习惯，该如何养成呢？

10
00:00:51,790 --> 00:01:01,660
According to a study published by the European Journal of Social Psychology, it takes an average of 66 days to form a new habit.
根据《欧洲社会心理学杂志》发表的一项研究，养成一个新习惯平均需要66天。

11
00:01:01,660 --> 00:01:07,110
However, relying only on determination may not be the answer.
不过，只靠决心可能并不够。

12
00:01:07,110 --> 00:01:13,050
Questioning why you want something to be the norm rather than relying on your resolve could be the key.
关键或许在于，问自己为何想让某件事成为常态，而非单纯依赖决心。

13
00:01:13,050 --> 00:01:17,290
Do you want to lose weight because you want to be healthier or feel more attractive?
你想要减肥，是为了更健康，还是为了让自己看起来更有魅力？

14
00:01:17,290 --> 00:01:24,280
The issue is, willpower could be subject to your mood – a bad mood may mean you don’t want to do something.
问题的关键是，意志力会受情绪影响——心情不好的时候，你可能就不想去做既定的事了。

15
00:01:24,280 --> 00:01:31,480
You should also avoid trying to change too much at once – remember that it’s a case of baby steps.
你还应该避免试图一蹴而就——要记住，凡事都要循序渐进。

16
00:01:31,480 --> 00:01:41,500
Giving up all your favourite foods, going to the gym, and stopping drinking at the same time will probably result in failure rather than sustainable practice.
一下子戒掉所有爱吃的食物、坚持去健身房锻炼、同时还戒酒，这样做很可能会失败，而非形成可持续的习惯。

17
00:01:41,500 --> 00:01:45,550
And don’t worry about failing – just start again!
而且别害怕失败——大不了重新开始！

18
00:01:45,550 --> 00:01:49,820
Finally, don’t do things outside your comfort zone.
最后，不要做超出自己舒适区的事。

19
00:01:49,820 --> 00:01:55,380
If you hate mushrooms, don’t persevere and try to add them to your diet just to be healthier.
如果你讨厌蘑菇，就不要为了健康而勉强自己吃。

20
00:01:55,380 --> 00:01:57,490
Eat something you like!
吃一些自己喜欢的食物就好！

21
00:01:57,490 --> 00:02:05,440
It might not be quick, but if you follow these tips, you may be able to change something for the better or kick a bad habit.
这个过程或许不会一蹴而就，但只要遵循这些建议，你或许就能做出积极的改变，或是戒掉某个坏习惯。
